# sentence_id = 94
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = So — just what I'm saying — don't, out of fear of this, grow weary of saving yourself; and don't let it trouble you to be in the awkward position you spoke of in court, that once you've gotten out you wouldn't know what to do with yourself.
# literal_translation = So that, which very thing I say, both not fearing these things may you grow weary to save yourself, and not — what you were saying in the court — let it become distressing to you, that you would not have [anything], having gone out, that you might use yourself [for].
