# sentence_id = 97
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = And besides, Socrates, I don't even think it's right of you to attempt this—betraying yourself when you could be saved—and to be so eager to bring about for yourself just the sort of fate that your enemies would wish, indeed did wish, for you, wanting to destroy you.
# literal_translation = Still further, O Socrates, not indeed just do you seem to me to attempt a deed, [namely] to betray yourself, [when] it being possible [for you] to be saved, and such things you hasten about yourself to become as indeed even your enemies would hasten and did hasten, wishing to destroy you.
