# sentence_id = 206
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Socrates: But these considerations you mention, about spending money and reputation and raising children, these, Crito, are in truth, I fear, just the concerns of the sort of people who carelessly put men to death and would just as carelessly bring them back to life again, if they could, acting with no sense at all—the concerns, that is, of the majority.
# literal_translation = Socrates: But the considerations which you mention, concerning both expenditure of money and reputation and rearing of children, [these], not as [being] truly these [things], O Crito, might be the considerations of those [men] easily killing and bringing back to life [again], if they were able, with no sense—[the considerations], that is, of these the many.
