# sentence_id = 207
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = But since the argument has turned out this way for us, nothing else needs to be considered except just what we were saying a moment ago: whether we would be acting justly in paying money and thanks to those who will get me out of here and in getting me out ourselves, or whether in truth we would be doing wrong by doing all this—we who are getting out and we who are getting them out.
# literal_translation = But to-us, since the argument thus turns out, nothing else must-be-considered than just-what we-were-saying just-now: whether just-things we-will-do, both money paying to-these the-ones who-will-lead-out me from-here, and [giving] thanks, and ourselves both leading-out and being-led-out, or in truth we-will-do-wrong, all these-things doing [0].
